  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility study for Diaspora engagement in energy access</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this assignment was to conduct a feasibility study to assess the extent to which Diaspora entities are engaged and can be mobilised to support energy transition initiatives in their countries of origin.Within this main goal, the action had the following three objectives:-	To inform and raise awareness among the Diaspora communities about the benefits of clean cooking in the households of their communities back home in terms of better health outcomes, time savings, and opportunities for economic development; -	To showcase success stories of diaspora engagement in the development of their countries of origin, either through market instruments (trade, entrepreneurship, investments etc.) or in other ways;-	To identify possible entry points and strategic niches through which the Diaspora can be effectively involved in further actions in the area in partnership with other stakeholders.This action targeted the Diaspora communities in the Netherlands from a number of selected countries</narrative>
  </description>
